  "_commit": {
    "id": "d0d5013c745ff88e36a2b9bd3dfec56f7c991c9e",
    "author": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "committer": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "message": "Add genome-wide HGNC-anchored master drug-target table builder\n\nNew R/genomeWideAnnot.R: downloadHgncTable()/getHgncGeneTable() (HGNC\ncomplete gene set as the gene-centric anchor, pinned quarterly snapshot\nfor reproducibility), buildHgncSymbolMap()/normalizeGeneSymbols() (DGIdb/\nTTD symbol-drift reconciliation), and buildGenomeWideDrugTargetTable()\n(checkpointed, resumable loop over the 4 annotation sources - the first\nfunction in this package to persist partial progress, needed at\ngenome scale). A single target-centric run answers both drug-target\ndirections at once. Excludes ChEMBL bioassay/PubChem, matching the\nearlier annotation/bioassay split.\n\nFixed two bugs found via live testing: HGNC's TSV needs standard\nCSV-style quote handling (quote = \"\" was leaving literal quote\ncharacters in alias data), and the batch runner's cache name must not\nbe a substring of another cache entry's name, since BiocFileCache's\nrname matching is substring-based by default and this was silently\nshadowing lookups of the HGNC file itself.\n",
    "time": 1784434660
  },
